The '''fifth series''' of ''[[The Great British Bake Off]]'' first aired on 6 August 2014, with twelve contestants.<ref name="digital">{{cite news |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s215/great-british-bake-off/news/a585984/fire-up-your-ovens-the-great-british-bake-off-return-date-confirmed.html#~oL11ELb7S7EU2j |title= Fire up your ovens! The Great British Bake Off return date confirmed |work=Digital Spy |date=23 July 2014  |author= Sam Rigby }}</ref> [[Mel Giedroyc]] and [[Sue Perkins]] presented the show and [[Mary Berry]] and [[Paul Hollywood]] returned as judges.  Twelve contestants competed in this series, and the competition was held in [[Welford Park]] in Berkshire.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.radiotimes.com/news/2014-08-06/bake-off-insiders-reveal-what-really-goes-on-inside-the-tent |title=Bake Off insiders reveal what really goes on inside the tent |author=Rosie Millard|date=6 August 2014 |work=Radio Times }}</ref> The series was won by [[Nancy Birtwhistle]], with Luis Troyano and Richard Burr finishing as runners-up.

The programme was moved from [[BBC Two]] to [[BBC One]] starting this year, but the Masterclass episodes remained on BBC Two.  A companion series, ''[[The Great British Bake Off: An Extra Slice]]'', hosted by comedian [[Jo Brand]], started this year on BBC Two.

The fifth series was broadcast as the first season on [[PBS]] in the United States.

