== Controversy ==

=== "Bingate" ===
In the fourth episode of the series, there was controversy over the events that preceded the elimination of contestant Iain Watters. During the final showstopper round contestants were tasked with producing a baked Alaska. Iain's ice cream was shown as having not set, and in a show of frustration, he threw his bake in the bin. The editing of the show suggested that another contestant, Diana Beard, had caused the failure by removing the ice cream from a freezer for her own ice cream, and the perceived "sabotage" resulted in a furore on social media networks.<ref>{{cite news|url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-great-british-bake-off-rocked-by-baked-alaska-sabotage-scandal-9695831.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-great-british-bake-off-rocked-by-baked-alaska-sabotage-scandal-9695831.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off rocked by Baked Alaska 'sabotage' scandal |work=The Independent |date=28 August 2014 |access-date=28 August 2014}}</ref>

More than 800 complaints were lodged with the BBC, and some complained to the communication watchdog [[Ofcom]].<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2014/aug/29/great-british-bake-off-ofcom-complaints-bbc-diana-beard-iain-watters |title=Great British Bake Off: Ofcom rules out investigation despite complaints |author=Jason Deans |date=29 August 2014 |work=The Guardian }}</ref> Some members of the cast, however, posted comments in support of Diana,<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2014/aug/28/great-british-bake-off-paul-hollywood-sue-perkins-bingate-iain-watters |title=Great British Bake Off: Paul Hollywood and Sue Perkins speak out on 'bingate' |publisher=guardian.com |date=28 August 2014 |access-date=28 August 2014}}</ref> and a BBC spokesman later issued a statement:

<blockquote>"As shown in the episode, Iain became the fourth baker to leave the tent because he didn't present Paul and Mary with anything to judge in the showstopper challenge and both judges were very clear about the reasoning behind the decision. Due to the extreme temperature in the tent that day, many of the bakers struggled to get their ice cream to set as seen in the episode. Diana removing Iain's ice cream from the freezer for less than a minute was in no way responsible for Iain's departure."<ref>{{cite web|url=http://metro.co.uk/2014/08/28/great-british-bake-off-2014-bbc-receives-over-500-bingate-complaints-while-justiceforiain-dominates-twitter-4849049/ |title=Great British Bake Off 2014: BBC receives over 500 'bingate' complaints while #justiceforiain dominates Twitter |publisher=metro.co.uk |date=28 August 2014 |access-date=28 August 2014}}</ref></blockquote>

The claim that his dish was only left out for a short time was, however, challenged by Iain Watters, who said that it was left long enough to ruin the dessert.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2014/aug/28/great-british-bake-off-ian-watters-speaks-diana-beard |title=Great British Bake Off: Iain Watters speaks out as Diana Beard quits |author=Hannah Ellis-Petersen |date= 28 August 2014 |work=The Guardian }}</ref>

Fellow contestant Jordan Cox criticized the show's production, claiming the freezers were not very good in quality, and were chosen only for their aesthetics.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s215/great-british-bake-off/news/a593577/jordan-cox-criticises-in-your-face-great-british-bake-off-team.html|title=Jordan Cox criticises "in your face" Great British Bake Off team|author = Ryan Love |date=31 August 2014  |work = Digital Spy}}</ref>

Diana Beard left the show before the next episode was filmed due to illness.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.radiotimes.com/news/2014-08-28/diana-quits-the-great-british-bake-off-2014 |title=Diana quits The Great British Bake Off 2014 |author=Susanna Lazarus|date= 28 August 2014 |work=Radio Times }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2014/aug/28/diana-beard-quit-bake-off-smell-taste |title=Diana Beard: I quit Bake Off after losing sense of taste and smell |author=Hannah Ellis-Petersen |date= 28 August 2014 |work=The Guardian }}</ref>

Beard later gave an interview to [[BBC Radio Shropshire]]: <blockquote>"I'm disappointed with the way it's been portrayed. I've been stitched up, haven't I? We were 12 amateur bakers, [there's] no prize money involved. Why would I sabotage Iain's Baked Alaska? This has made it look like some cutthroat competition. I think someone's culpable for the editing, really."<ref name="beardexit"/> </blockquote> Beard also said that Iain's ice cream had been out of the freezer for no more than 40 seconds, and that her conscience was clear.<ref name="beardexit">{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/entertainment-arts-28964737|title=Great British Bake Off: Diana Beard's exit announced|date=29 August 2014|work=BBC}}</ref>

The incident would later be referenced by contestant Iain Ross (also from Belfast) in [[The Great British Bake Off series 16|series 16]]. Tasked to create a showstopper '[[vacherin glacé]]' consisting of ice cream and meringue, Ross was inspired by his and Watters' shared first name and hometown, creating a 'Bingate Redemption' dessert using the same flavours of Watters' baked Alaska.

=== Innuendo ===
A number of viewers complained to the BBC feedback show ''[[Points of View (TV series)|Points of View]]'' in the fifth series about the "constant smutty remarks" from the presenters Mel and Sue.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/great-british-bake-off-2014-viewers-complain-about-smutty-innuendos-as-we-pick-the-best-9752461.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/great-british-bake-off-2014-viewers-complain-about-smutty-innuendos-as-we-pick-the-best-9752461.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off 2014: Viewers complain about 'smutty' innuendos |work=The Independent |author=Jess Denham |date=24 September 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/features/bake-off-2014-from-a-good-forking-to-erect-biscuits--our-favourite-great-british-innuendos-9782163.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/features/bake-off-2014-from-a-good-forking-to-erect-biscuits--our-favourite-great-british-innuendos-9782163.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off innuendos: we pick our favourites |author=Matilda Battersby |date=8 October 2014 |work=The Independent }}</ref> This series was seen as having more innuendos than previous ones; some reviewers noted the "extra pinch of saucy spice" and "the increasingly filthy-minded hosts Mel Giedroyc and Sue Perkins",<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/blogs-the-papers-28684187 |date=7 August 2014 |title=Boris Johnson's 'Commons comeback', Bake Off 'smut' and who is James Corden?
|author= Andy McFarlane |work=BBC }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.thetimes.com/culture/tv-radio/article/tv-review-the-great-british-bake-off-57xr8925fmr |title=TV Review: The Great British Bake Off |author=Andrew Billen |date=7 August 2014 }}</ref> though Series 3 winner John Whaite argued that innuendo is part of what made the show a success,<ref>{{citation |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/11115090/Soggy-bottoms-and-hot-buns-why-the-Bake-Off-thrives-on-innuendo.html |title=Soggy bottoms and hot buns: why the Bake Off thrives on innuendo |author=John Whaite |date= 23 September 2014 |work=The Daily Telegraph }}</ref> while Paul Hollywood described the innuendo as banter in the spirit of the [[Carry On (franchise)|''Carry On'' films]] and is a part of British culture,<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/great-british-bake-off/11141937/Great-British-Bake-Off-smut-Its-just-a-bit-of-banter-says-Paul-Hollywood.html |title=Great British Bake Off smut? It's just a bit of banter, says Paul Hollywood |author= Anita Singh |date=6 Oct 2014 |work= Daily Telegraph}}</ref> a view shared by others.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2014/oct/08/great-british-bake-off-sprinkling-smut-sexual-innuendo |title=Why the Great British Bake Off needs a sprinkling of smut |author=Martin Rowson |work=The Guardian |date= 8 October 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=http://blogs.telegraph.co.uk/culture/harrymount/100076314/great-british-bake-off-smut-ooh-matron-why-innuendo-comes-so-easily-for-the-british/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141008034609/http://blogs.telegraph.co.uk/culture/harrymount/100076314/great-british-bake-off-smut-ooh-matron-why-innuendo-comes-so-easily-for-the-british/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=8 October 2014 |title=Great British Bake Off smut: Ooh, Matron! Why innuendo comes so easily for the British |author= Harry Mount |date=6 October 2014 |work=The Daily Telegraph}}</ref>

== Post-show careers ==
Richard Burr's book on baking, ''BIY: Bake it Yourself'', was released on 16 August 2015.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.westerndailypress.co.uk/Bake-s-Richard-Burr-new-book-BIY-Bake/story-27811512-detail/story.html |title=Great British Bake Off's Richard Burr on his new book BIY: Bake It Yourself|work= Western Daily Press |date= 19 September 2015 }}</ref>

Luis Troyano also wrote a book, ''Bake It Great'', released on 20 August 2015.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/extras/indybest/10-best-cookbooks-by-great-british-bake-off-contestants-james-morton-ruby-tandoh-a6680291.html |archive-url=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20220618/https://www.independent.co.uk/extras/indybest/10-best-cookbooks-by-great-british-bake-off-contestants-james-morton-ruby-tandoh-a6680291.html |archive-date=18 June 2022 |url-access=subscription |url-status=live |title=Great British Bake Off: 10 best cookbooks |author=Pippa Bailey Monday |date=5 October 2015 |work=The Independent}}</ref> He died of oesophageal cancer in November 2020 at the age of 48.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/news/tv/entertainment/2020-11-03/luis-troyano-dead-great-british-bake-off.html |title=Great British Bake Off finalist Luis Troyano dies aged 48 |author=Minnie Stewart |date=3 November 2020 |work=Radio Times}}</ref>

Chetna Makan has written a baking book ''The Cardamom Trail,'' released on 21 March 2016, as well as a cookbook ''Chai, Chaat & Chutney: A Street Food Journey Through India'', published on 6 July 2017.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.thebookseller.com/news/gbbo-semi-finalist-chetna-makan-publish-second-cookbook-490676 |title=GBBO semi-finalist Chetna Makan to publish second cookbook |author=Katherine Cowdrey |date=20 February 2017 |work=The Bookseller}}</ref><ref>{{cite book| url=https://www.octopusbooks.co.uk/books/detail.page?isbn=9781784722876| title=Chai, Chaat & Chutney| publisher=[[Mitchell Beazley]]| access-date=2017-08-11| website=octopusbooks.co.uk| date=5 September 2017| isbn=9781784722876}}</ref> Makan has continued to write cookbooks focused on Indian cooking, with ''Chetna's Healthy Indian, Chetna's Healthy Indian Vegetarian, and Chetna's 30-Minute Indian'' published in 2019, 2020, and 2021 respectively.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Chetna Makan|url=https://www.amazon.com/kindle-dbs/entity/author/B074QNL241?_encoding=UTF8&node=283155&offset=0&pageSize=12&searchAlias=stripbooks&sort=author-sidecar-rank&page=1&langFilter=default#formatSelectorHeader|access-date=2021-12-18|website=www.amazon.com|language=en-us}}</ref>

Martha Collison has written two baking books, ''Twist,'' released on 14 July 2016, and ''Crave'', published 13 July 2017 with Harper Collins.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.harpercollins.com/author/cr-123733/martha-collison/|title=Martha Collison}}</ref> She also has a weekly column with [[Waitrose]]<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.waitrose.com/home/recipes/baking/bake-with/martha-collison.html|title=Martha Collison Baking Recipes &#124; Waitrose}}</ref> and is a charity ambassador for [[Tearfund]].<ref>https://www.tearfund.org/en/media/press_releases/tv_bakers_martha_and_will_team_up_with_tearfund_to_host_baking_events_this_october/ {{Dead link|date=February 2022}}</ref>

[[Nancy Birtwhistle]] released her first book ‘Sizzle and Drizzle’<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.nancybirtwhistle.co.uk/sizzle-and-drizzle-book/|title=Sizzle and Drizzle – Nancy Birtwhistle}}</ref> in 2020. She released her second book, Clean & Green: 101 Hints and Tips for a More Eco-Friendly Home in 2021.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bookdepository.com/Clean-Green-Nancy-Birtwhistle/9781529049725|title=Clean & Green : Nancy Birtwhistle : 9781529049725}}</ref>

== Ratings ==
The series started with its highest ratings for its opening episode after its move to BBC One, with over 7 million tuning in according to overnight figures.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2014/aug/07/great-british-bake-off-bbc1-ratings |title=John Plunkett |date= 7 August 2014 |work=The Guardian }}</ref> This is adjusted to 8.5 million for its 7-day final viewing figure, making this its second most-watched episode after previous year's final.<ref>{{cite news |url= http://www.broadcastnow.co.uk/ratings/bbc1s-in-the-club-delivers/5076466.article |title=BBC1's In The Club delivers |date= 21 August 2014 |author= Stephen Price|work=Broadcast Now }}</ref> In the fourth episode, 8.1 million watched the original broadcast,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/news/a593041/great-british-bake-off-climbs-to-huge-ratings-of-810m.html |title=Great British Bake Off climbs to huge ratings of 8.10m |author= Tom Eames |date=8 Aug 2014 |work=Digital Spy }}</ref> but the "bingate" controversy gained the show a further 2 million viewers on the [[BBC iPlayer]] catch-up service, giving the show the biggest ever audience with 10.248 million viewers for the episode.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/great-british-bake-off/11088494/Great-British-Bake-Off-shock-as-no-one-is-eliminated.html |title=Great British Bake Off shock as no one is eliminated |author=Hannah Furness |date= 10 September 2014 |work=The Daily Telegraph}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.mirror.co.uk/tv/tv-news/great-british-bake-draws-highest-4170904 |title=Great British Bake Off draws highest ever ratings as 10.3 million viewers tune in |author=Nicola Methven |date= 5 September 2014 |work=Mirror }}</ref> The final of the show gained an overnight viewing figure of 12.29 million,<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s215/great-british-bake-off/news/a602261/great-british-bake-off-final-is-most-watched-non-sporting-tv-event-of-year.html |title=Great British Bake Off final is most-watched non-sporting TV event of year |author=Ben Lee |date=9 October 2014 |work=Digital Spy |access-date=9 October 2014 |archive-date=10 October 2014 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20141010070158/http://www.digitalspy.co.uk/tv/s215/great-british-bake-off/news/a602261/great-british-bake-off-final-is-most-watched-non-sporting-tv-event-of-year.html |url-status=dead }}</ref> and a consolidated average figure of 13.5 million, the highest viewing figure for a non-sporting event of the year on UK TV, after [[2014 FIFA World Cup]]'s England vs Uruguay match.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/media/2014/dec/17/the-great-british-bake-off-tv-ratings-2014 |title=The Great British Bake Off rises to top of most-watched TV of 2014 so far |author=Tara Conlan|date= 17 December 2014 |work=Guardian }}</ref> Series 5 had an average of viewing figure of 10.1 million.<ref>{{cite news |url=http://www.broadcastnow.co.uk/ratings/bbc1-rises-to-the-challenge/5082034.article |title=BBC1 rises to the challenge|date=22 January 2015 |author= Stephen Price |work=Broadcast }}</ref>

Official episode viewing figures are from [[BARB]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.barb.co.uk/whats-new/weekly-top-30|title=Weekly Top 30 Programmes|publisher=[[Broadcasters' Audience Research Board]]|access-date=16 September 2015}}</ref>

